---
// Analytics preferences: a working switch for website analytics in this browser.
// The switch writes PREFERENCE_KEY (scripts/analytics-events.mjs) to local storage, and
// scripts/analytics.mjs reads it before starting PostHog and again before every event.
// This page itself never loads analytics.
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { LEGAL_UPDATED, LEGAL_UPDATED_LABEL, CONTACT_EMAIL, legalPage } from '../lib/legal';
import { PREFERENCE_KEY } from '../scripts/analytics-events.mjs';

export const prerender = true;

const description = 'Turn Kuchi website analytics off or on for your browser. Analytics uses no cookies and never stores your IP address; Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control always turn it off. What the MCP server records about agents.';
const toc = [
  { id: 'switch', label: 'Website analytics switch' },
  { id: 'how-it-works', label: 'How the switch works' },
  { id: 'signals', label: 'Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control' },
  { id: 'website', label: 'What website analytics records' },
  { id: 'mcp', label: 'What MCP server analytics records' },
  { id: 'questions', label: 'Questions' },
];
---
<LegalLayout title="Analytics preferences — Kuchi" description={description} toc={toc} jsonLd={legalPage('WebPage', '/analytics-preferences', 'Kuchi analytics preferences', description)}>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <h1>Analytics preferences</h1>
    <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: <time datetime={LEGAL_UPDATED}>{LEGAL_UPDATED_LABEL}</time></p>
    <p>Kuchi counts how its website is used so we can make it better. That counting uses no cookies, never stores your IP address and is not tied to you. If you would still rather not be counted, switch it off here. Kuchi works exactly the same either way.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <h2 id="switch">Website analytics switch</h2>
  <div class="pref-card" data-analytics-pref data-state="on">
    <div class="pref-row">
      <div>
        <p class="pref-label" id="pref-label">Website analytics in this browser</p>
        <p class="pref-status" id="pref-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">On. Page views, clicks and page speed are counted anonymously.</p>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="pref-switch" role="switch" aria-checked="true" aria-labelledby="pref-label" aria-describedby="pref-status" data-analytics-switch>
        <span class="pref-thumb" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <noscript><p class="pref-note">The switch needs JavaScript. Without JavaScript, Kuchi’s analytics cannot run either, so nothing is counted.</p></noscript>
  </div>

  <h2 id="how-it-works">How the switch works</h2>
  <p>When you switch analytics off, this page saves <code>{PREFERENCE_KEY}</code> = <code>off</code> in your browser’s local storage. Every Kuchi page checks it before analytics starts, and again before each event is sent. While it is off, no analytics request leaves your browser: the analytics script is not loaded, and pages already open in other tabs stop sending events at once.</p>
  <p>Saving this choice is strictly necessary to respect it, so it needs no consent. It stays on your device and is never sent to us or to analytics. The choice applies to this browser on this device; use the switch again in other browsers. If you clear your browser’s site data, the choice is cleared too and analytics returns to its default, on. If your browser does not allow this page to save the choice, the page tells you; Global Privacy Control, described below, then works in every case.</p>

  <h2 id="signals">Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control</h2>
  <p>If your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, website analytics is off whatever this switch says, and the switch shows that. Under California law we treat Global Privacy Control as a request to opt out of the sale and sharing of personal information, which Kuchi never does in any case.</p>

  <h2 id="website">What website analytics records</h2>
  <p>When analytics is on, we record page views, clicks on buttons and links, reference viewing, filter use (how long a search is and how many results it gave, never the words), connection attempts, page performance and script errors, through this site’s own <code>/relay</code> path to PostHog in the United States. Nothing is stored in your browser for analytics, your IP address is not saved with any event, and we do not record sessions or what you type. The full list is in the <a href="/privacy#website-analytics">privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="mcp">What MCP server analytics records</h2>
  <p>This switch is about the website. AI agents that connect to Kuchi’s MCP server are counted separately, on the server. For each tool call we record which tool ran, how long it took, whether it failed, the name and version of the connecting client, its country, the catalog search terms and filters used, which reference was requested, and a one-line description of the task if the agent chooses to send one.</p>
  <p>Agents’ calls are not tied to a person. Kuchi has no accounts and receives no names or email addresses, and the server does not record IP addresses. The product details an agent sends to plan or check a remake are used for that one answer and never stored or sent to analytics. Calls are grouped only by a random token for one connection, which says nothing about who is behind it. More in the <a href="/privacy#mcp-analytics">privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="questions">Questions</h2>
  <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}?subject=Privacy`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. See also the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>, the <a href="/terms">terms</a> and the <a href="/legal">legal notice</a>.</p>
  <p><a href="/">Back to the collection ↗</a></p>
</LegalLayout>

<script>
  import { PREFERENCE_KEY, readPreference, analyticsAllowed } from '../scripts/analytics-events.mjs';

  const card = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-analytics-pref]');
  const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-analytics-switch]');
  const status = document.getElementById('pref-status');
  const storage = (() => { try { return window.localStorage; } catch { return null; } })();
  const privacy = { globalPrivacyControl: (navigator as Navigator & { globalPrivacyControl?: boolean }).globalPrivacyControl, doNotTrack: navigator.doNotTrack };
  const signal = privacy.globalPrivacyControl ? 'Global Privacy Control' : privacy.doNotTrack === '1' ? 'Do Not Track' : null;

  const MESSAGES = {
    on: 'On. Page views, clicks and page speed are counted anonymously.',
    off: 'Off. This browser sends no analytics to Kuchi.',
    signal: (name: string) => `Off. Your browser sends ${name}, so analytics stays off whatever this switch says.`,
    unsaved: 'Your browser did not let this page save the choice. Turn on Global Privacy Control in your browser to keep analytics off.',
  };

  function render(note?: string) {
    if (!card || !button || !status) return;
    const off = !analyticsAllowed(privacy, readPreference(storage));
    card.dataset.state = off ? 'off' : 'on';
    button.setAttribute('aria-checked', String(!off));
    button.disabled = Boolean(signal);
    status.textContent = note ?? (signal ? MESSAGES.signal(signal) : off ? MESSAGES.off : MESSAGES.on);
  }

  button?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (signal) return;
    const turnOff = readPreference(storage) !== 'off';
    try {
      if (!storage) throw new Error('No storage');
      if (turnOff) storage.setItem(PREFERENCE_KEY, 'off');
      else storage.removeItem(PREFERENCE_KEY);
    } catch {
      render(MESSAGES.unsaved);
      return;
    }
    render(readPreference(storage) === (turnOff ? 'off' : 'on') ? undefined : MESSAGES.unsaved);
  });
  // Follow a change made on this page in another tab.
  window.addEventListener('storage', (event) => { if (event.key === PREFERENCE_KEY || event.key === null) render(); });
  render();
</script>

<style>
  .pref-card { border: 1px solid var(--k-line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 20px; margin: 0 0 24px; background: var(--k-wash); }
  .pref-row { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; }
  .pref-label { font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 4px !important; }
  .pref-status { margin: 0 !important; color: var(--k-muted); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .pref-note { margin: 12px 0 0 !important; font-size: 14px; color: var(--k-muted); }
  .pref-switch {
    flex: none; position: relative; width: 52px; height: 30px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--k-line);
    background: var(--k-muted); cursor: pointer; padding: 0; transition: background-color 160ms cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1);
  }
  .pref-switch[aria-checked="true"] { background: var(--k-accent); }
  .pref-switch:disabled { cursor: not-allowed; opacity: 0.6; }
  .pref-switch:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--k-accent); outline-offset: 3px; }
  .pref-thumb {
    position: absolute; top: 3px; left: 3px; width: 22px; height: 22px; border-radius: 50%; background: #fff;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.25); transition: transform 160ms cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1);
  }
  .pref-switch[aria-checked="true"] .pref-thumb { transform: translateX(22px); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .pref-switch, .pref-thumb { transition: none; } }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .pref-row { align-items: flex-start; } }
</style>
